; messages.vla - the engine's own refusals, the cart family (ENGINE.1's second
; slice, 2026-10-09; docs/SPEC.md section 4.7). One (message <id> <number> "<source>"
; "<template>") form an entry, the shape of the language's catalog, read by
; its mechanism, vla_lang::messages::Catalogue, which fills each {slot}; an id
; this file does not hold is the language's (the grid, view and calc families).
; Each text names its target as sheet!addr where it has one, so that the host
; prints the module's words alone, and leaves the row's line to the record's
; line field. Embedded at build time by engine/src/cartridge.rs; its test holds
; every id the engine raises to this file.

(message cart-manifest-invalid 5 "Alonzo-Cart" "The cartridge's manifest {what}. A cartridge begins with (cartridge \"name\" ...), the name in lowercase letters, digits and hyphens, and gives (spec ...), (title ...), (rate ...), (screen ...) and (seed ...) once each, nothing defaulted (docs/SPEC.md section 7.2).")
(message cart-spec-unsupported 5 "Alonzo-Cart" "The cartridge is written to (spec {spec}), and this engine reads (spec 1), (spec 2), (spec 3), (spec 4), (spec 5), (spec 6), (spec 7), (spec 8) and (spec 9); a cartridge written to a later page waits for an engine that reads it.")
(message cart-screen-outside 5 "Alonzo-Cart" "{target} is outside the Screen's window, {window}, which the manifest's (screen ...) declares; without a Camera sheet the Screen holds cells only inside that window (docs/SPEC.md section 3.1).")
(message cart-palette-invalid 5 "Alonzo-Cart" "{what}. A plane cartridge's Palette holds sixteen rows, column A the index from 0 to 15 in order and column B its color as #RRGGBB, or a formula that computes one (docs/SPEC.md section 3.2).")
(message cart-device-cell-formula 5 "Alonzo-Cart" "A formula cannot go into {target}: {cells} are the host's to write, and hold values, since the host would write over a formula there and nobody would see why (docs/SPEC.md section 3).")
(message cart-device-cell-outside 5 "Alonzo-Cart" "{target} is outside the layout of the {sheet} sheet, {layout}: a device sheet holds its cells where docs/SPEC.md section 3 lays them out, so that a later version can add a row without colliding with a cartridge.")
(message cart-formula-volatile 5 "Alonzo-Cart" "The formula in {cell} calls {function}, which reads the wall clock or the dice, so no replay could reproduce it. The engine's clock is the frame in Clock!B1 and its dice the seed in Clock!B3; a random number is a formula of the seed and the last frame (docs/SPEC.md section 3.5).")
(message cart-write-derived 5 "Alonzo-Cart" "A derived write cannot go into {target}: {cells} are the host's to write, so a derived write lands only in a value cell the host does not write (docs/SPEC.md section 3.9).")
(message cart-source-unexpanded 5 "Alonzo-Cart" "The file holds a {form} form, so it is a cartridge's source, which the pass expands into the rows a load takes (docs/SPEC.md section 7.8): expand it, and load the cartridge the pass writes.")
(message cart-too-large 5 "Alonzo-Cart" "The file is {size} bytes, over the {limit} a cartridge may be (docs/SPEC.md section 10), so it is not loaded; a host writes no save over it, so that every save it writes loads again.")
(message cart-write-clock 5 "Alonzo-Cart" "{target} {what} (docs/SPEC.md section 3.5).")
(message cart-command-invalid 5 "Alonzo-Cart" "{what}. A cartridge's commands are named in column A of its Commands sheet, from row 2, in lowercase letters, digits and hyphens, each name once: the name a page lists and the Input sheet's twentieth row holds (docs/SPEC.md section 3.10).")
(message cart-format-invalid 5 "Alonzo-Cart" "{what}. A cartridge written to (spec 9) says a file's lines on its Format sheet, in values: the file's type in B1, its comment's leader in B2, the row a sheet's first line stands on in B3 and LF or CRLF in B4; then, from row 6, a sheet of its own in column A beside a line of the file in column B, the line written out with a hole for each column (docs/SPEC.md section 3.11).")
(message cart-file-unread 5 "Alonzo-Cart" "The file was not read: {what}. A file is read by the lines the cartridge's Format sheet says, each line by the first that reads it whole, and nothing is loaded from a file a line of which none reads (docs/SPEC.md section 3.11).")
(message cart-file-unwritten 5 "Alonzo-Cart" "The file was not written: {what}. A row is written by the line the cartridge's Format sheet says for its sheet, and nothing is written of a grid a row of which no line says (docs/SPEC.md section 3.11).")
